{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/935922-could-monopoly-replace-chess-amongst-younger-vampires","id":935922,"title":"Could Monopoly replace Chess Amongst younger vampires?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-22T21:10:44-07:00","id":935922,"title":"Could Monopoly replace Chess Amongst younger vampires?","content":"I hear chess referenced in both requiem and Masquerade as something that elders do a lot.<br /> <br /> but wondered back to a lecture I got in a personal Finances class I took in College (No I didnt get my Degree)<br /> <br /> &quot;Monopoly teaches you most of what you need to know to survive in the world of finances&quot; <br /> <br /> Ive taken that to heart and tried to relearn the rules <br /> <br /> Allready know rules for chess but trying to master strategy.<br /> <br /> Sorry if it seems a silly question just found I've seen chess referenced so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T21:38:26-07:00","id":935930,"title":"","content":"Not really. There's a tried and true strategy to Monopoly, whereas there's more possible games of chess than stars in the known universe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How to win at Monopoly \u2013 a simple strategy:<br /> Always buy Railroads; never buy Utilities (at full price)*<br /> For every other property type, only buy them to complete a monopoly or to prevent opponents from completing one. Often this may mean buying as many properties as you can early in the game, but watch your cash reserves.<br /> At the beginning of the game, focus on acquiring a complete C-G [Color Group: all 2 or 3 properties of the same color] in Sides 1+2, even if it means trading away properties on Sides 2+3. After acquiring one of these C-Gs, build 3 houses as quickly as possible: no more houses, no less!<br /> Once your first C-G starts to generate some cash, focus on completing a C-G and building 3 houses in Sides 3+4.<br /> Note: 3 houses is the &quot;sweet spot&quot; in the game as shown in Table 1 below. That\u2019s where you\u2019re making the best use of your money.<br /> Single properties are the least good investment if you don\u2019t build on them.<br /> The only exception to the above rules are when you need to acquire stray properties to prevent your opponents from completing their Color-Groups to accomplish the above strategy. <br /> <br /> Jail can be good. Stay in Jail as long as you can if an opponent owns a monopoly \u2013 at that point in the game, moving around the board will likely lose you money. Until that happens, though, pay the $50 and leave Jail as soon as possible: you need to be in the property acquisition race and collecting your $200 salary.<br /> One interesting exception: Do you need St. James or Tennessee Aves to complete your C-G? Then stay in Jail and try to get out by rolling doubles: doing so will increase your chances of landing on those squares by about 25%.<br /> The 5 best starting positions are \u2013 in order:<br /> All 4 railroads<br /> One reason why this is the best starting point: the revenue flow from railroads is much more constant over time whereas some of the other properties may have the same ROI but they come with bigger payouts over longer time spans. Owning 3-4 railroads is a cash cow: it will bring a continuous flow of money that can fund your monopolies.<br /> 3 houses on each of the orange Color-Group (St James/Tennessee/New York)<br /> 3 houses on each of the light blue C-G (Oriental/Vermont/Connecticut)<br /> 3 houses on each of the light purple C-G (St Charles/States/Virginia)<br /> A hotel on each of the dark purple C-G (Mediterranean /Baltic)<br /> This option gives by far the worst return of the 5 starting positions; in fact, until you get 4 houses, this C-G is the worst investment in the game!<br /> However, his option does have 2 advantages: it is the cheapest of the 5 and it only has 2 properties so owning the entire C-G may be easier, especially in large games. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T22:53:24-07:00","id":935949,"title":"","content":"Monopoly is really less of a game and more of an elaborate work of satire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T22:59:17-07:00","id":935951,"title":"","content":"Presumably there's more modern games that could take up that place in the vampire's lair reserved for a chess board they play every twenty years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-23-2016, 02:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T23:42:09-07:00","id":935958,"title":"","content":"Im curious do you think the special guest speaker at my personal financer class, was an idiot, he seemed reasonable to me","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T00:02:16-07:00","id":935966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/935922-could-monopoly-replace-chess-amongst-younger-vampires?p=935958#post935958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im curious do you think the special guest speaker at my personal financer class, was an idiot, he seemed reasonable to me</div> </div> </div> </div>Hard to answer objectively without knowing who the speaker was, or having attended the talk or knowing which university endorsed it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T01:03:34-07:00","id":935981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/935922-could-monopoly-replace-chess-amongst-younger-vampires?p=935966#post935966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hard to answer objectively without knowing who the speaker was, or having attended the talk or knowing which university endorsed it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fair enough my Professor was a wealthy enough man, wealth enough he qualified for a $3,000,000 Credit limit credit card, which he showed to the class showed the kind of cool benefits it would give, showed how it was a rip off.<br /> <br /> Told us what to look for that the best credit card offers arent the ones we get int he Mail...<br /> <br /> also said our Values have a strong impact on what kinds of job we take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T02:59:03-07:00","id":936001,"title":"","content":"When people say things like that, they usually explain the metaphor a bit. I doubt he meant literally, learn monopoly and then you'll be better at personal finance.<br /> <br /> Same way, learning Chess won't literally make you more strategic. But it makes for a neat metaphor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T03:17:37-07:00","id":936006,"title":"","content":"Monopoly is, as Charlaquin pointed out, bitterly satirical. The monopolizing entrepreneurs go to jail and escape easily with no longer-term consequences (it's dated too). I can't imagine a bunch of vampires squatted around a board, cursing as the Nosferatu primogen takes all the railroards. That said, I <i>like </i>vampires with human hobbies and foibles, but without deft handling it might reduce your chronicles to a weird vampire comedy. <br /> <br /> I can actually see poker and similar card games being far more popular with vampires of all ages - lots of bluffing, for a start. Chess gets a lot of press because, well, <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/SmartPeoplePlayChess\" target=\"_blank\">Smart People Play Chess</a> and it's an old game which makes sense for elders.The <i>real </i>elders are playing senet, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T04:00:42-07:00","id":936016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/935922-could-monopoly-replace-chess-amongst-younger-vampires?p=936006#post936006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can actually see poker and similar card games being far more popular with vampires of all ages - lots of bluffing, for a start.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's an interesting sub-text to that (and a lot of these games actually), that they appear to be about one thing when they're actually about another. I gather professional poker players generally don't really bother trying to read each others body language, it's about calculating probability in your head based on available information.<br /> <br /> That seems a pretty abt metaphor for Vampire: the neonates trying to bluff each other whilst the Elder wins because they know how the game is actually played.<br /> <br /> There's also something interesting about really old elders playing Senet, a game that's basically chance. It might say something about their view of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T04:57:40-07:00","id":936027,"title":"","content":"Pente is a modern board game with enough complexity that it can stand in for chess in the danse macabre metaphor, especially as number of players increase making keeping track of piece capture opportunities more challenging. It does lack the element of divine hierarchy found in chess (The Great Chain of Being resulting feudal structure as above so below, thus monarchy working through ranked intermediaries) but it could be said each Pente piece represents an intermediary and they are all equally sacraficable. The Great Chain of Being was well reflected in the Cain myth in classic world of darkness with its generation mechanic, Camarilla and Sabbat hierarchies and generally Christian centric paradigm and Pente is far most postmodern with its metaphor being abstracted to the point that those that get it may feel existential dread.<br /> <br /> At least if I was a Mekhet teaching my childer how to play, that's what I'd tell them. But hey I like leaving classic world of darkness in my game under Blackdog publishing because roleplaying is hitting mainstream culture and leaving it out creates a whole in the world. Also a gaming universe with gaming universes inside other gaming universes makes me smile. (of course with 28 years of actively being a Dungeon Master/Referee/Game Master/Lore Keeper/Storyteller it could be argued any character which isn't specialized in gaming and story crafting wouldn't be 'me' in a meaningful sense)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-23-2016, 08:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T05:10:41-07:00","id":936033,"title":"","content":"Putting aside the analysis of the actual board game, I can't see games like Monopoly being a replacement for chess, simply because of the random nature of the game. Dice and random chance feature heavily in the game beyond the basic strategies to win. Its simply less engaging in polishing your skills or challenging opponents.<br /> <br /> Plus, Monopoly exaggerates one of the worst weaknesses of the vampire existance - ennui. It can be a good metaphor for being a vampire that, once you collect up your territories and build them up, you circle endlessly around the board with little penalty or things to do. Most vampires play games to get away from ennui, while Monopoly basically exalts it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T06:20:53-07:00","id":936052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/935922-could-monopoly-replace-chess-amongst-younger-vampires?p=935958#post935958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im curious do you think the special guest speaker at my personal financer class, was an idiot, he seemed reasonable to me</div> </div> </div> </div>What? No. The fact that it's satire is part of the reason that it's a good microcosm of finance. Finance doesn't make for a good board game. People always joke that no one actually likes monopoly because it feels bad to loose, it feels bad to win, it takes a million years, and you can usually tell who's going to win long before it's over, but you still have to keep going through the motions because there's just enough of a random element that the game might just swing in your favor. The taking a million years part is mostly due to house rules that people use like pooling tax money and giving it to who ever lands on free parking, but the other complaints are pretty accurate. And even the prevalance of the house rule just goes to show how monopoly isn't actually fun. The free parking rule is a misguided attempt to introduce a feel-good moment into an otherwise complete downer of a game, and to give the underdogs a chance to make a comeback. But it causes huge problems by occasionally re-introducing huge amounts of money into the system, which makes it take much longer to actually bankrupt everyone so the game can end. That's the thing, the game is <i>supposed</i> to be a miserable experience, because it was designed to be social commentary on the nature of business, not to be an enjoyable game to play. It's unsurprising that there's lessons to be learned about finance from the game, because its design prioritizes effective commentary over good gameplay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-23-2016, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T10:13:43-07:00","id":936140,"title":"","content":"I am now imagining an Indian elder, of the Dragons or the LeS,who trolls/tests prospective students by requiring them to play a mathematically unwinnable game of Chutes and Ladders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T13:19:50-07:00","id":936208,"title":"","content":"Old Vampires are few and far. Chess makes for a fantastic intellectual duel.<br /> <br /> Neonates are more common, compared to Elders. As such, they should play Diplomacy, a game that demands strategic thinking but doesn't suggest that you can take it all for yourself without manipulating a few pawns.<br /> <br /> Monopoly should be discussed as we are doing now. Playing it is like getting a coffee: a pretense to get together and enjoy some conversation. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T14:05:03-07:00","id":936231,"title":"","content":"I could see totally see neonates playing other board games, though. Catan, Carcassonne, Cthulhu Wars...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T14:13:00-07:00","id":936236,"title":"","content":"I'd expect Monopoly to result in too many Frenzies. Playing it with humans is bad enough...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T19:52:44-07:00","id":936378,"title":"","content":"Munchkin and Illuminati by SJgames would probably be suitably backstabby for neonate vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T22:48:59-07:00","id":936428,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of an ancient gamer. In life they were idle rich with a passion for popular games. This passion has not diminished with age, and the Game Master has everything from an ancient set of throwing bones, jackals and hounds, medieval chess board, to things like a modern board game library(which of course has Monopoly. Consider also that Jenga could be played to it's fullest, most extreme potential by vampires), extensive(ly haunted) arcade hall with impossibly high scores all made long ago, a personal theater with a complete library of console games spanning their relatively recent history, and a cutting egde VR colosseum where the newest Call of Duty is played all the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","user":"JTroy","date":".  Typos. Oops. 07-24-2016, 01:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T22:55:18-07:00","id":936433,"title":"","content":"Thinking further into it, I think that videogames in general, especially ones that require precision and reflexes, would be very popular among young vampires with celerity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T11:51:45-07:00","id":936638,"title":"","content":"Sticking to board games, I think Settlers of Catan or Carcassonne would be preferred by neonates in the thematic department. Chess is a game of elders who have all the pieces available. Catan is a game for neonates, where you have to use what you've been given to win.<br /> <br /> However, like with elders it would vary a lot. I'd say that those the Ventrue embrace would already be interested in or adept at chess, and so it would appear among all ages of vampire, while others would tend towards draughts as an intergenerational game. I can also see a small backgammon scene among vampires.<br /> <br /> I'd also expect vampires to have their own board games we don't. I'd imagine some abstraction of politics and the hunt, with pieces such as the Primogen, the Bishop, the Mortal, maybe even pieces like the Ghoul or the Politician. The board would represent both physical location and allegiance, with the goal to get all the pieces on your team.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T13:30:39-07:00","id":936694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/935922-could-monopoly-replace-chess-amongst-younger-vampires?p=936638#post936638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can also see a small backgammon scene among vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see some of the eldest elders preferring this and other Tables variants over chess. Imagine an ancient Mekhet playing a game of Senet with a Mummy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-24-2016, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T16:55:30-07:00","id":936795,"title":"","content":"What's with all these western games? How about some Shogi or Go?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T17:04:04-07:00","id":936803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/935922-could-monopoly-replace-chess-amongst-younger-vampires?p=936795#post936795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's with all these western games? How about some Shogi or Go?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure Go would also be quite popular. I don't know Shogi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T17:19:15-07:00","id":936814,"title":"","content":"We are talking about younger vampires, and even in the east globalization has brought computer and video games and other sports. I don't see young vampires going into chess, shogi or go if they weren't involved in it before their Embrace. I have to agree with TwoDSix on their views about board games.<br /> <br /> But most likely the elders place for a thousand year old chess board carved from the bones of extinct animals would for a neonate be inhabited by a laptop or desktop. In addition to allowing one to play chess, shogi, go, World of Warcraft, poker, and variants of basically every game there is, it contains direct access to vast repositories of information gathered from hundreds and thousands of years of human experience across the globe. Plus you can always use it to reach out and ask for advice from someone on the opposite side of the planet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T17:30:31-07:00","id":936818,"title":"","content":"What about good old Mafia? <br /> Board games and video games are actually an interesting thing, because in a lot of them, a Vampire will not be superior to a mortal in any way. I could see a Touchstone based around that idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T03:11:42-07:00","id":936991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/935922-could-monopoly-replace-chess-amongst-younger-vampires?p=936795#post936795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's with all these western games? How about some Shogi or Go?</div> </div> </div> </div> To be honest, Go just slipped my mind. I do see it as the equivalent of chess for Kindred in China and Asia, while in Europe and America it's more of a niche game but still played. I don't know enough about Shogi to make a statement on it.<br /> <br /> On the subject of a Touchstone based around games, I can say that I'd allow one representing your gaming group. Take about one night out a week to play some board games with your old friends and it would work like normal. I'd hesitate to allow one based on video games, as they are moving away from all being in the same room interacting with each other, so the interaction isn't as personal (YMMV, but board games are just better).<br /> <br /> Also, keep in mind the differences between the minds of an old and young vampire. Yes, a young vampire is more likely to make sure they have space for a computer than for a board game, but I'm sure that several will also have a stack of games. It'll just be a travel chessboard rather than one carved from the bones of their dead ghouls, assuming they like chess.<br /> <br /> On the subject of computers, bare in mind that quite a few elders, especially among the Ordo Dracul, will have learnt to use desktops in the same way they will have learnt to use a phone, especially after GUIs made them easier to use. A neonate's tech advantage is that they probably have a laptop and so can carry it around with the, as well as a smartphone and possibly a desktop. Imagine the scene, vampires waiting for an audience with the Prince, two elders in a heated chess match, but calm, and one neonate getting annoyed at Flappy Bird, while another is sitting with his laptop out going over the notes emailed to him by his research partner touchstone.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T04:29:56-07:00","id":937003,"title":"","content":"How much of that whole &quot;elders stuck in the past&quot; trope is still relevant? Given the Old+New theme going on, 2e makes it sound like even older vampires have kept up with modern technology - luddites aren't exactly savvy city predators, after all. It doesn't sound as much like a neonate advantage when both the Invictus and Carthians have merits that focus on using modern technology to manipulate mortals and maintain their power and prestige, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T05:27:30-07:00","id":937013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/935922-could-monopoly-replace-chess-amongst-younger-vampires?p=936795#post936795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's with all these western games? How about some Shogi or Go?</div> </div> </div> </div>Shatranj, Rithmomachy, and Tafl, or no deal.<br /> <br /> But really, Chess &quot;wins&quot; for Kindred, at least in the West for a very simple reason - it's portable and easy to learn, but mastering it is <i>hard</i>. It gives you something to do in your unlife, at the very least. It also has <i>strong</i> connotations as a &quot;thinking man's&quot; game - otherwise, you'd see a <i>lot</i> more card games.<br /> <br /> I'm amazed we don't see any Vampires taking the time to master Bridge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T06:23:36-07:00","id":937038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/935922-could-monopoly-replace-chess-amongst-younger-vampires?p=936006#post936006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Monopoly is, as Charlaquin pointed out, bitterly satirical. The monopolizing entrepreneurs go to jail and escape easily with no longer-term consequences</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I\u00b4m Spanish. I would wish the current politicians, bankers and rich businessman were <i>merely </i>playing Monopoly with my country. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 07-25-2016, 09:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T07:45:46-07:00","id":937084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/935922-could-monopoly-replace-chess-amongst-younger-vampires?p=937013#post937013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shatranj, Rithmomachy, and Tafl, or no deal.<br /> <br /> But really, Chess &amp;quot;wins&amp;quot; for Kindred, at least in the West for a very simple reason - it's portable and easy to learn, but mastering it is <i>hard</i>. It gives you something to do in your unlife, at the very least. It also has <i>strong</i> connotations as a &amp;quot;thinking man's&amp;quot; game - otherwise, you'd see a <i>lot</i> more card games.<br /> <br /> I'm amazed we don't see any Vampires taking the time to master Bridge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Knowing how to play bridge (and mahjong) actually got one of my neonate characters in and out of some sticky situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T09:29:56-07:00","id":937136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/935922-could-monopoly-replace-chess-amongst-younger-vampires?p=937003#post937003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> How much of that whole &quot;elders stuck in the past&quot; trope is still relevant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Little of it, they seem to exist as unique and backwards individuals. Even in torpor minds adapt to prepare vampires to hunt in the present. P105 'During her slumber, she experiences strange, nonsensical dreams that keep her mind active and exercised. Usually, this means she\u2019s prepared to adapt to a new world.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Given the Old+New theme going on, 2e makes it sound like even older vampires have kept up with modern technology - luddites aren't exactly savvy city predators, after all. </div> </div> </div>It's expanded further in the Moving Up section, but the book repeatedly mentions that vampires are adept at adapting to the new times. At least as they would be in life. Just as there are luddites in the real world, there are those among the Kindred. P164, 'A few ancient vampires resist the change of technology, but enterprising Kindred of all ages embrace it as a means to connect with the future.'<br /> <br /> Such vampires are making a willing decision to be anachronistic, unless there's some other cause for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-25-2016, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T09:30:36-07:00","id":937137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/935922-could-monopoly-replace-chess-amongst-younger-vampires?p=937038#post937038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I\u00b4m Spanish. I would wish the current politicians, bankers and rich businessman were <i>merely </i>playing Monopoly with my country. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hence dated :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T06:24:42-07:00","id":941896,"title":"","content":"I can see some forward-minded Elders sitting their childer down and making them play video games like Democracy or some of the Paradox grand strategy games, like Crusader Kings II. Democracy for &quot;how to effectively lord over the masses,&quot; and CKII for &quot;How to preserve your lineage while lording over the masses.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T08:06:15-07:00","id":941951,"title":"","content":"I don't know about Monopoly, do people really play it that much ?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/935922-could-monopoly-replace-chess-amongst-younger-vampires?p=936638#post936638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also expect vampires to have their own board games we don't. I'd imagine some abstraction of politics and the hunt, with pieces such as the Primogen, the Bishop, the Mortal, maybe even pieces like the Ghoul or the Politician. The board would represent both physical location and allegiance, with the goal to get all the pieces on your team.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yes, that and the gaming nut vampire. A vampire would have invented a game that is really popular with vampires, it's the game you have to play and be good at to be one of the cool ones.<br /> <br /> Maybe, kind of like Monopoly in its own way, it's full of vampire culture references, with the big covenants being a playstyle or something. The game would be modded to reflect the current times when big events happen like the Carthian movement emerging of the Circle of the Crone being formed. It's technically a breach of masquerade to show it to mortals. That game could also be so ridiculously intricate and complex you'd need the longevity and unique mindset of a vampire to really master it. Maybe it's more than just a board with pieces and involves actually going out and do things. Some old feud between two elders could just be a friendly (as friendly as it can be between old vampires) game and those who take part in it and risk their unlives don't realize it.<br /> <br /> Another question, is it just a game or did the creator have an ulterior motive ? It is a game made by an undead freak after all, could it be that safe ? Does mastering it simply involve letting go of part of your human logic, requiring you to lower your humanity to be really good at it ? Is it cursed in some form (the creator could have created a number of original sets that they rigged in some way) ? Why ? Does it have prophetic elements to it and vampires are slowly making the connection between it and real world events ?<br /> <br /> The creator is a malkavian, how would all those uppity elders who lord it over neonates who don't understand the rules of the game react if they knew that ? Would they lash out in some irrational fear that it may give them malkavia ? Would they try to cover up the truth because they really love that game but couldn't deal with the shame of being addicted to an entertainment made by one of those nutjobs ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T08:50:19-07:00","id":941977,"title":"","content":"They probably play Werewolf the Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T11:44:45-07:00","id":942125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/935922-could-monopoly-replace-chess-amongst-younger-vampires?p=936006#post936006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <i>real </i>elders are playing senet, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually agree with this - Senet, mancala, derrah, and tafl. The hell is chess? Sounds like one of them cell go games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T05:46:58-07:00","id":942654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/935922-could-monopoly-replace-chess-amongst-younger-vampires?p=941951#post941951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, yes, that and the gaming nut vampire. A vampire would have invented a game that is really popular with vampires, it's the game you have to play and be good at to be one of the cool ones.<br /> <br /> Maybe, kind of like Monopoly in its own way, it's full of vampire culture references, with the big covenants being a playstyle or something. The game would be modded to reflect the current times when big events happen like the Carthian movement emerging of the Circle of the Crone being formed. It's technically a breach of masquerade to show it to mortals. That game could also be so ridiculously intricate and complex you'd need the longevity and unique mindset of a vampire to really master it. Maybe it's more than just a board with pieces and involves actually going out and do things. Some old feud between two elders could just be a friendly (as friendly as it can be between old vampires) game and those who take part in it and risk their unlives don't realize it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I don't like the idea of having to go outside and so things for the game, but I do see it as a game where outside influences affect it, and played over multiple evenings. So there are rules for the number of days which have passed between sessions, the covenant leading the city affects how pieces move between various spaces. Heck, I see the colour of dice you roll as something that influences the game.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo it's not a game where you have to do things in the 'real world', but in longer games vampires might pull strings and politic to get an advantage at the next meetup. All based around a simple core idea and setup.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does mastering it simply involve letting go of part of your human logic, requiring you to lower your humanity to be really good at it? </div> </div> </div> I actually assumed that this would be the case. It requires a different mindset to see how the various strategies and moves actually work. Why does the Lancea Sanctum strategy require you to leave the Bishop exposed on turn 3? Why does a Carthian game require you to spread your pieces out and abandon Elyssium? What purpose does the sewer have except for being a slower route than the street.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T09:10:43-07:00","id":942744,"title":"","content":"Hum... just a game where you play for x time on set dates and if you dont show up you pass your turn or something would be interesting to vampires. Especially if it was meant to be played by a lot of people at once. Allow out of game trading for in game benefits. &quot;Ill give you a boon if you give me x card.&quot;<br /> <br /> You could build a story off of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T10:28:16-07:00","id":942799,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://boardgamegeek.com/boardgame/13456/vampire-prince-city\" target=\"_blank\">Prince of the City</a> could be a good tool to abstract this hypothetical vampire board game, and give players something to physically manipulate and play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T10:55:39-07:00","id":942811,"title":"","content":"Well as a personal anecdote of mine i have a very pretentious intellectual uncle, he was the dean of a architecture university and one evening he came by my house and watch my friends and i play pokemon TCG and he sneer and comment how &quot;chess was the true game of strategy and that the were a thousand possible moves etc etc pretentious bs&quot;.<br /> <br /> My then 12 year old self look at him and told him that &quot;while, yes it a game of strategy its also a dead game of strategy because nothing changes everything goes as planned always while in this (pokemon) a bad hand can throw my plan to hell and i have to see a way to think quickly with the little resources i had. Real life usually dont deal with everything going as plan&quot; i love pissing him off.<br /> <br /> Now my 25 year old self with add this to the reasoning &quot;and then there is *that* asshole who buys everysingle card he needs to maximize some OP combo he read somewhere on the internet but if could beat a full blastoise op deck with my fire deck so can you&quot;<br /> <br /> So i would say vampire play magic! Its a good way for the filthy rich ventrue to spend some millions of dollars every few years.<br /> <br /> More on topic, i could see not all elder buying into chess and play something else. Monopoly.....teg if they wanna risk frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 08-03-2016, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T16:35:20-07:00","id":943093,"title":"","content":"I've always imagined Elders would be more partial to playing Go rather than chess, since it's even more complex. But then, I'm biased towards go, personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11756-razikale","name":"Razikale","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T20:07:27-07:00","id":943325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/935922-could-monopoly-replace-chess-amongst-younger-vampires?p=941977#post941977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They probably play Werewolf the Forsaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>That kind of begs the question. Do White Wolf, Onyx Path and their various games exist in ChroD?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T21:07:13-07:00","id":943369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/935922-could-monopoly-replace-chess-amongst-younger-vampires?p=943325#post943325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That kind of begs the question. Do White Wolf, Onyx Path and their various games exist in ChroD?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like classic World of Darkness' 'Black Dog' with their weird variants. I'd probably not have Vampire the Requiem, but would have vampire role-playing games. Really, I think it would be on a setting by setting basis. Requiem could be the result of a break in the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> It's an interesting change in dynamic between vampires and werewolves. Even disregarding the old stereotypes of cities and wildernesses and cold beauty versus hot passion. Both are predators, creatures of the night, though werewolves aren't confined to it. Werewolves have packs, which aren't entirely free of backstabbing but probably good for teaching a coterie how to rely on, support, and trust one another. Then there's the Requiem. There's no handbook for being dead, vampires have to decide for themselves what to do with their unlives. But werewolves basically have a divine mandate, a primal urge to hunt that lives in every molecule of their being. And they're rewarded for what they do. A vampire might be screwed over by politics, but whether you're vilified or not, the lunes will mark you with that Renown. There's arguably even a difference in their deaths. For vampires it's a source of fear and dread, but for werewolves dying heroically can be a glorious thing.<br /> <br /> I could see vampires digging it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T03:23:32-07:00","id":943516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/935922-could-monopoly-replace-chess-amongst-younger-vampires?p=943325#post943325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That kind of begs the question. Do White Wolf, Onyx Path and their various games exist in ChroD?</div> </div> </div> </div>They do if you want to. Like pretty much anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T06:21:06-07:00","id":943577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/935922-could-monopoly-replace-chess-amongst-younger-vampires?p=943325#post943325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That kind of begs the question. Do White Wolf, Onyx Path and their various games exist in ChroD?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing's stopping you, but at the very least, I'd prefer it if the wider setting I'm playing in at the moment didn't exist as a game within the setting. So no CofD when playing Chronicles, but oWoD might exist etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T10:44:08-07:00","id":943706,"title":"","content":"In my CofD, White Wolf and the cWoD exist, but nobody in the supernatural community can figure out where they got their info, or why they would distort that info in the way they did. It's considered a very odd sort of masquerade breach and all attempts to investigate white wolf turn up nothing. What the supernaturals don't know that while white wolf themselves don't know the supernatural actually exists, several high level video game industry folks do, as a result of the overzealous suppression of world of darkness video games (in other words, the guys behind Bloodlines know, as do the folks involved in the canceled heart of gaia game.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T03:55:51-07:00","id":944223,"title":"","content":"Young Mekhet love playing Khet.<br /> <br /> It has Egyptian motifs. And it's laser mirror chess. <i>Egyptian laser mirror chess.</i><br /> <br /> Roll Wits+Composure to not go &quot;pchuuuu&quot; when you fire your laser.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T05:48:10-07:00","id":944257,"title":"","content":"Do youngsters these days even know what Monopoly is?<br /> <br /> Yes, yes. Now get off my lawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10978-azenogoth","name":"Azenogoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10978_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T07:43:21-07:00","id":944304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/935922-could-monopoly-replace-chess-amongst-younger-vampires?p=944223#post944223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has Egyptian motifs. And it's laser mirror chess. <i>Egyptian laser mirror chess.</i></div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bI tend to find that description of it incredibly misleading. It's actually not as balanced as chess, first move advantage is much greater and there's at least one hard to counter early game strategy (I found moving second required certain moves when playing it), compared to chess where both sides are fairly balanced (white has a slight advantage, but at least at a casual level the difference becomes smaller as the game goes on) and most early game strategies have at least a few easy counters.<br /> <br /> Not that Khet is bad, it can be fun, it's just not as balanced a game as chess (and generally faster as well, which for me is a downside as I enjoy my hour long games of chess full of lots of strategizing and occasionally minutes between moves).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T08:17:50-07:00","id":944328,"title":"","content":"I've always thought Diplomacy would make a good game for Vampires to play against each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12028-questerr","name":"Questerr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T18:38:38-07:00","id":946623,"title":"","content":"I feel like the satire aspect of Monopoly is what vampires would enjoy the most about it. I could see them playing Poker, too. Sadly, most elders don't appreciate the balance and complexity of X-Wing. <br /> <br /> In my personal ChroD, the game itself doesn't exist but Black Dog Publishing did, but is now defunct and is seen by most RPG players as an alternately embarrassing/amusing relic of the 90s. Mage: The Awakening does exist, as a dark yet hopeful game about occult superheroes, and in-universe it was published by a group of Mages from the Heirs of Atlantis legacy to promote their Supernal Symbology Paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}